{"name":"Bonne Nuit","hex":"#3a4866","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bonne","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A French nursemaid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bonne"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bonne Nuit (Jersey)","blocks":[{"text":"Bonne Nuit is a small natural harbour in the Vingtaine du Nord, Saint John, Jersey, Channel Islands. Both Bonne Nuit in French and Bouonne Niet in Jèrriais mean \"good night\", referring to the shelter sailors could rely on by overnighting in the harbour. The bay nestles between the headlands of Frémont in the West and La Crête in the East."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/JY012_bba.jpg/330px-JY012_bba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonne_Nuit_(Jersey)"},{"title":"Nuit","blocks":[{"text":"Nuit is a goddess in Thelema, a Western esoteric quasi-religion. Nuit is the speaker in the first chapter of The Book of the Law, the sacred text written or received in 1904 by Aleister Crowley. Nuit is based on the Ancient Egyptian sky goddess Nut, who in Egyptian mythology arches over her brother/husband, Geb. She is usually depicted as a naked woman who is covered with stars."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuit"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/JY012_bba.jpg/500px-JY012_bba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/JY012_bba.jpg/1280px-JY012_bba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/JY012_bba.jpg/500px-JY012_bba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJY012_bba.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Bouonne_Niet_